# 5. FLUTTER TECHNOLOGY STACK

Use a modern, stable Flutter release compatible with the development environment.

Verify the installed Flutter and Dart versions before choosing dependencies.

Do not upgrade unrelated development tools automatically.

## Core technologies

- Flutter
- Dart
- Material 3 as a foundation, customized for the Guides Nepal brand
- Cupertino conventions where appropriate for iOS
- Riverpod for state management
- GoRouter for navigation
- Dio for networking
- Freezed for immutable models and unions
- json_serializable for JSON serialization
- flutter_secure_storage for sensitive local storage
- Drift with SQLite for structured offline caching when justified
- Flutter's built-in asset and localization infrastructure

## Additional packages

Evaluate and use suitable maintained packages for:

- Image caching
- Responsive layouts
- Animation
- Form validation
- Internationalization
- Date and time selection
- Maps
- Push notifications
- Deep linking
- Analytics
- Crash reporting
- Secure authentication
- File and image selection
- Accessibility testing

Select packages according to actual requirements.

Before adding a package, verify:

- Maintenance status
- License
- Compatibility with current Flutter/Dart
- iOS and Android support
- Security considerations
- Transitive dependencies
- Performance impact

Do not add multiple packages that perform the same job.

## Architecture pattern

Use a pragmatic combination of Clean Architecture and feature-first organization.

```text
Presentation
     │
     ▼
Controller / Riverpod Provider
     │
     ▼
Use Case / Application Logic
     │
     ▼
Repository Interface
     │
     ▼
Repository Implementation
     │
     ├── Remote Data Source
     │
     └── Local Data Source
```

Keep the architecture understandable.

Do not introduce unnecessary abstractions into simple features.

